{"name":"Jungle Noises","hex":"#36716f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jungle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, lush, undeveloped, humid forest, especially in a tropical region, thick with vegetation and wildlife; a tropical  rainforest.","Any uncultivated tract of forest or scrub habitat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(Of musical beat, rhythm, etc.) resembling the fast-paced drumming of traditional peoples of the jungle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle"},{"term":"noises","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of noise"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of noise"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noises"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jungle","blocks":[{"text":"A jungle is an area of land covered with dense forest and tangled vegetation, usually in tropical climates. Application of the term has varied greatly during the past century. Because jungles occur on all inhabited landmasses and may incorporate numerous vegetation and land types in different climatic zones, the wildlife of jungles cannot be straightforwardly defined."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg/330px-%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle","wikidata":"Q191086"},{"title":"Noise","blocks":[{"text":"Noise is sound, chiefly unwanted, unintentional, or harmful sound considered unpleasant, loud, or disruptive to mental or hearing faculties. From a physics standpoint, there is no distinction between noise and desired sound, as both are vibrations through a medium, such as air or water. The difference arises when the brain receives and perceives a sound. Acoustic noise is any sound in the acoustic domain, either deliberate or unintended."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Noise_Research_Program_on_Hangar_Apron_-_GPN-2000-001457.jpg/330px-Noise_Research_Program_on_Hangar_Apron_-_GPN-2000-001457.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noise","wikidata":"Q179448"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/500px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/1280px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/500px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jungle on Tioman Island, Malaysia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATioman_Rainforest.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/500px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/1280px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg/500px-Puerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"El Yunque National Forest in Puerto Rico, the only tropical rainforest managed by the U.S. National Forest Service","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuerto_Rico_El_Yunque_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Mosnticulo_de_los_anranjos.jpg/500px